## Purpose

This document defines the backend architecture for Project Athena.

It describes how trusted server-side application logic shall process authenticated requests, enforce authorization, validate input, execute financial business rules, coordinate persistence, create audit records, process imported files, generate reports, and manage background work.

The backend must preserve financial correctness, security, explainability, and auditability while remaining modular and maintainable.

