## Domain Services

Domain Services shall implement financial rules that span entities or repositories.

### Transaction Normalization Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Normalizing dates
- Normalizing signed amounts
- Normalizing descriptions
- Mapping account context
- Producing canonical transaction candidates

### Duplicate Detection Service

Responsibilities may include:

- File fingerprinting
- Transaction fingerprinting
- Duplicate-candidate scoring
- Retry protection
- Explicit duplicate resolution

### Transfer Matching Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Matching opposite-signed transactions
- Matching account ownership
- Evaluating date proximity
- Preventing income and expense inflation
- Preserving transfer relationships

### Classification Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Applying precedence rules
- Evaluating merchant rules
- Producing explanation metadata
- Identifying conflicts
- Creating review items

### Budget Calculation Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Calculating available income
- Applying zero-based allocations
- Calculating actual spending
- Handling rollovers
- Preserving closed-period history

### Debt Payoff Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Calculating payoff progress
- Modeling scenarios
- Projecting payoff dates
- Documenting assumptions
- Separating actual payment history from projections

### Net Worth Calculation Service

Responsibilities may include:

- Aggregating dated asset values
- Aggregating dated liabilities
- Preventing double counting
- Creating immutable snapshots

