## Import Processing

The import pipeline is one of Athena's most security-sensitive and financially significant workflows.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Upload[Upload]
    ValidateFile[Validate File]
    Identify[Identify Source]
    Parse[Parse Rows]
    Normalize[Normalize]
    Fingerprint[Fingerprint]
    Detect[Detect Duplicates and Transfers]
    Classify[Apply Rules]
    Review[Create Review Items]
    Persist[Persist Authoritative Records]
    Summarize[Create Import Summary]
    Audit[Create Audit Record]

    Upload --> ValidateFile
    ValidateFile --> Identify
    Identify --> Parse
    Parse --> Normalize
    Normalize --> Fingerprint
    Fingerprint --> Detect
    Detect --> Classify
    Classify --> Review
    Classify --> Persist
    Review --> Persist
    Persist --> Summarize
    Summarize --> Audit
```

Import processing shall:

- Treat files as untrusted
- Validate format and size
- Validate content
- Prevent path manipulation
- Use source-specific parsers
- Preserve source lineage
- Reject malformed records safely
- Prevent duplicate effects
- Produce explicit row outcomes
- Record processing version
- Record import status
- Avoid sensitive logging
- Support safe retry

