## Security Considerations

Backend security risks include:

- Broken authorization
- Row Level Security bypass
- Service-role misuse
- Insecure file parsing
- Injection
- Sensitive logging
- Duplicate financial effects
- Missing audit records
- Client-supplied ownership manipulation
- Insecure direct object references
- Preview environment access to production
- Unvalidated external responses
- Overly broad storage permissions

Required controls include:

- Server-side authorization
- Owner-scoped repositories
- Runtime validation
- Parameterized queries
- Private storage
- Least privilege
- Audit logging
- Idempotency
- Safe error handling
- Secrets management
- Automated security testing
- Dependency scanning
- Static analysis
- Secret scanning

---

## Performance Considerations

Backend performance objectives include:

- Efficient monthly imports
- Paginated transaction queries
- Indexed reporting paths
- Avoidance of unnecessary full-table scans
- Batched persistence where safe
- Efficient dashboard aggregates
- Clear background-job boundaries
- Measured optimization rather than premature complexity

Performance improvements must not compromise authorization, correctness, or auditability.

